#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""PA19 v6_3 admission/ownership. Single normal3.5GiB sampled group threshold, COUNT<=2; NO automatic retries.
v6_3 = v6 with: SUP_PATH/SUP_SHA pin supervise_pa19_v6.py (v3 plus the safety-checked delayed reap); every full_gate
refuses at/after the lease's frozen policy admission cutoff (missing cutoff refuses); Capacity.supervise refuses
a group whose 2400 s budget does not fit before the chunk deadline (frozen native end minus cleanup); a signal
observed by the supervisor sets the owner cancel flag.
v6_3 = v6_2 with the SUP pin on supervise_pa19_v6.py (signal-blocked finalization); runtime logic otherwise unchanged.
Every admission gate and inventory share one persistent-veto registry (old m2k1 plus new m2k3 markers).
Local supervise_pa19_v6 copies the reviewed r3 with one ownership callback only; the exact Popen remains retained
until explicit wait/reaping AND group quiescence. Native groups contain no /bin/ps/setuid helper.
Accounting amendment: immutable exact census age<=600s, refreshed at chunk start/expiry/waits>600s; reserve all
planned remaining outputs plus256MiB. Residual: the bound covers this route's writes and assumes no other lane
writer adds>256MiB within600s. statvfs, STOP/count/deadline and contract binary checks remain per-admission fresh.
Sampled RSS thresholds are NOT kernel instantaneous hard caps. Unknown measurements refuse; safety holds persist.
"""
